   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "Spot indices are market averages, not quotations. FAK and surcharge figures are carriers' published tariffs, base port to base port; contract and NAC rates differ. Colour key: red means more expensive for the cargo owner, green means cheaper.",
      "decorations": [
       {
        "type": "ITALIC",
        "italicData": true
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "paragraphData": {}
  },
  {
   "type": "HEADING",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "What changed on our side of the canal",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "headingData": {
    "level": 2
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "HEADING",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "Asia–Med services re-route through Sokhna and Damietta",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "headingData": {
    "level": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "PARAGRAPH",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "The Premier Alliance's MD1 Asia–Med service has moved back to the Suez routing. Its revised rotation calls at Sokhna on the way in and at Damietta in both directions, starting with Yang Ming's 11,714 TEU YM Trust from Ningbo on 13 November. The round voyage now takes 84 days with 12 ships, against 16 ships on the Cape routing. For Egyptian importers this means more direct Asia calls on the Red Sea side.",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "paragraphData": {}
  },
  {
   "type": "PARAGRAPH",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "Source: ",
      "decorations": [
