  {
   "type": "HEADING",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "Money is dearer; prices are rising more slowly",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "headingData": {
    "level": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "PARAGRAPH",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "The Central Bank of Egypt raised rates by 100 basis points on 29 October, its first hike since March 2024. The overnight deposit rate is now 20.0% and the lending rate 21.0%. That raises the cost of financing inventory and trade credit. Urban inflation eased to 12.7% in October, its lowest since January. The MPC meets again on 17 December, and the IMF's Extended Fund Facility for Egypt expires on 15 December, with its final review under way. Importers holding stock should build the higher carrying cost into Q1 landed-cost estimates now.",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "paragraphData": {}
  },
  {
   "type": "PARAGRAPH",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "Source: ",
      "decorations": [
       {
        "type": "ITALIC",
        "italicData": true
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "EnterpriseAM, 1 and 10 Nov 2026",
      "decorations": [
       {
        "type": "ITALIC",
        "italicData": true
       },
       {
        "type": "LINK",
        "linkData": {
         "link": {
          "url": "https://enterpriseam.com/egypt/2026/11/01/cbe-hikes-for-the-first-time-since-march-2024-raising-rates-100-bps-and-moving-its-inflation-target-to-4q-2027/",
