  },
  {
   "type": "PARAGRAPH",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "type": "TEXT",
     "nodes": [],
     "textData": {
      "text": "USTR has formally extended its suspension of the Section 301 port fees on Chinese-built and Chinese-operated vessels. The suspension now runs to 11:59 p.m. US Eastern time on 9 January 2027, so the fees could come back from 10 January unless Washington acts again. The fee falls on ship operators, not on cargo directly, so for now carriers calling the US with these ships have nothing to pass on. The decision has only been postponed.",
      "decorations": []
     }
    }
   ],
   "paragraphData": {}
